---
alwaysApply: true
---
Assume the following environment variables are set in a file named .env at the root of the project:
Variables without an equals sign are set but hidden to you.

# Essential Environment Variables for Job Portal
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values

# Database - MongoDB Connection
# Replace with your values from slack
MONGO_DB_USER=test_db_user
MONGO_DB_PASSWORD=
MONGO_DB_URL=mongodb+srv://${MONGO_DB_USER}:${MONGO_DB_PASSWORD}@job-portal.rwdy5sh.mongodb.net/?appName=job-portal
MONGO_DB_NAME='job-portal'

# ChromaDB Configuration
CHROMA_PC_PATH=./chroma_db
ALLOW_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# AWS Credentials (if we use bedrock)
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
# Non permament (12hours)
AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=""
BEDROCK_MODEL=amazon.nova-lite-v1:0

# OPENAI (if we use chatgpt models)
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Langsmith (if we use langsmith)
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
LANGSMITH_TRACING="true"
LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT="https://api.smith.langchain.com"
LANGSMITH_PROJECT="job_portal"

# CORS - Frontend URL
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Next.js
# Local Machine
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000
# Docker
NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://backend:8000
